+# Cancelling a Booked Visit Stays Out of Scope
+
+**Status:** Accepted. Narrows NG-5 of [ADR-2026-08-08](2026-08-08-non-goal-deletion-and-visit-amendment.md).
+
+## Context
+
+NG-5 declined both changing and cancelling a visit once booked, confirmed deliberate on 2026-08-08. That ADR made any narrowing a recorded owner decision with its own non-goal ADR.
+
+The owner requested correction of a booked visit on 2026-11-05. The intake decision reads: "Non-goal NG-5 is narrowed: cancelling a booked visit stays out of scope, but correcting its date and description is now in."
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Keep NG-5 whole.** Rejected by the owner decision quoted above.
+2. **Open both correction and cancellation.** Rejected: the owner kept cancellation out of scope.
+3. **Narrow NG-5 to cancellation alone** (chosen).
+
+## Decision
+
+Correcting a booked visit's date and description is in scope. Cancelling a booked visit stays out of scope. NG-4 is untouched: deleting a visit stays out of scope.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- REQ-VIS-003 adds the correction under the same rules as booking.
+- The sample no longer treats a booked visit as immutable; owner, pet, and visit details all correct forward.
+- No cancellation or deletion flow is planned. Opening either takes another recorded owner decision.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-5
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed NG-5 row.
+- [PRD Visits](../prd.md#req-vis-003) — the correction requirement.
